  "body": "Follow-up to #871 (refusal ghost for part-way refusals). The #871 PR adopted the ghost where the moves are in hand and the frame is already mapped to world by `run_job`. The remaining part-way refusals each need a frame map or a merge first, so they were listed in `docs/decisions/871-refusal-ghost-rest.md` rather than swept:\n\n- **finishing3d raster / rings / swarf** (`raster.rs` `parallel`, `rings_and_tail`, `swarf_multi`): Rotary contour and parallel run these on frame-LOCAL facets (`multiaxis/rotary.rs` calls of `finishing3d::waterline` / `swarf`). First add `.map_err(GenError::without_ghost)` (or a `to_world` map) at those rotary calls, then adopt `with_ghost_moves(b.moves())`.\n- **Rotary links and posing** (`rotary_links.rs` `radial_relink`, `rotary.rs` `posed`): rotary-local frame. Needs `f.to_world` plus the tip offset.\n- **Face under an area turn** (`generate.rs` `turn_path(face_over(..)?, -turn)`): the refusal's spot (already today) and any ghost are in the turned frame. Map the spot and ghost back through `turn_path(-turn)`.\n- **Cross drill app-side laws** (`cross_spindle.rs` `rapids_clear`, `cross_holder` on the spindle-shifted `t`): carry the ghost by the same shift `in_world` uses.\n- **Nested refusals** (`machining3d/entry.rs` `pocket3d_air_split` material leg, `run_rest` rest ladder; `generate.rs` stitched contour runs): the inner refusal already carries its own ghost and `with_ghost` keeps it. Prepend the outer moves to it, which needs a small `Ghost` merge.\n- **Multiaxis stamp / swarf link / curve walk, the rotary gate, the fixture route**: these are one-liners, but each needs its frame checked (posed or unposed world).\n\nDone means: each site above either hands back its partial path in world coordinates (pinned by a test that its ghost lands where the part is) or is listed in a decision file with the reason. No generator's successful output changes, so goldens stay byte-identical.\n\nEffort is `high` because it touches generator code (safety floor), even though the change is display-only.\n\nPart of #261 (follow-up to #871).\n",
